# Tracer: numeric membership of a literal tuple coordinate at the special-property stage.
# Before: (0,0)(1) $in C needed the finite-function membership strategy.
# Consequently a tuple equality's generated scalar child could fail its numeric WD.
# Now: read the selected literal coordinate and retain its closed membership calculation.
# Boundary: the whole call must be WD; wrong indices and false numeric carriers reject.
# Evidence: target/release/litex -lang en -strict -f examples/proof_nodes/atomic/by_known_special_property/literal_tuple_numeric_coordinate.lit
# Rust: tests/add_zero_builtin.rs. This new evidence has no Lean replay yet.

(0, 0)(1) $in C
(0, 3 / 2)(2) $in Q
(i, 0)(1) $in C

have pair R × R = (0, 3 / 2)
pair(2) $in Q
